# RJ45 Connector

A generic eight-pin RJ45-style board connector. The body covers eight by seven
hole pitches, with pins 1–8 arranged from left to right along the bottom edge.

The required north-facing cable-access region covers six by six holes and is
shifted two holes above the component origin. It is centered horizontally over
columns 1–6.

RJ45 connector footprints and auxiliary-pin functions vary. Verify the pin
numbering against the physical connector before wiring it.
